---
import Admin from '../../../layouts/Admin.astro';
---
<Admin title="Photos" active="photos">

  <h1 class="adm-h1">Photos</h1>
  <p class="adm-lede">
    Photographs of finished tools, work in progress and the shop floor, for the
    Our Work section on the homepage.
  </p>

  <div class="adm-wip">
    <span class="adm-tag">Being built</span>
    <h2>Uploading is not switched on yet</h2>
    <p>
      The page you are looking at is real, the upload is not. It needs one thing
      from the Azure side first — a token that lets this panel commit your
      photographs to the site. Until that exists, pressing an upload button
      would fail silently, so there is no upload button.
    </p>
    <p>
      <b>You can get ahead of it now.</b> Photographs are the single biggest
      thing missing from the site, and taking them does not wait on any of this.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="adm-brief">
    <h2>What to photograph</h2>
    <p class="adm-brief-lede">
      Around twenty is right. A tight set of real work reads as confidence; a
      hundred snapshots reads as filler. Daylight, no styling, a phone is fine.
    </p>
    <ul class="adm-list">
      <li><b>Finished tools on the bench</b> — the thing a customer is buying. The most important shot on this list.</li>
      <li><b>A die set open</b>, showing the punches and the die block. Engineers look at this and can tell whether you know what you are doing.</li>
      <li><b>Something mounted in a press</b>, ideally mid-job.</li>
      <li><b>The wire-cut or the jig borer running.</b> Machines with work in them, not machines standing idle.</li>
      <li><b>A jig or fixture with the component sitting in it.</b> Shows the fit, which is the whole point of a fixture.</li>
      <li><b>The shop floor, wide.</b> One honest photograph of the room.</li>
      <li><b>Your team working.</b> People buy from people. This matters more than it sounds.</li>
      <li><b>Inspection</b> — a gauge or a height master in use.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="adm-brief-foot">
      Avoid: anything under a customer NDA, anything with a drawing number or
      part name visible that is not ours to show, and anything blurry. A blurry
      photograph of good work does the work a disservice.
    </p>
  </section>

</Admin>
